1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,652
Text messages get read within
minutes, which makes them powerful.

2
00:00:04,652 --> 00:00:09,570
In this lesson, you'll create SMS
templates, see how WhatsApp templates work,

3
00:00:09,570 --> 00:00:12,764
and send a broadcast, all
while staying compliant.

4
00:00:12,764 --> 00:00:17,299
SMS is included on the Growth and
Pro plans, and WhatsApp is an add-on.

5
00:00:18,172 --> 00:00:20,779
Before we click anything, three rules.

6
00:00:20,779 --> 00:00:23,866
Only text people who
agreed to hear from you.

7
00:00:23,866 --> 00:00:25,443
Always say who you are.

8
00:00:25,443 --> 00:00:27,913
And always tell them how to opt out.

9
00:00:27,913 --> 00:00:30,725
If you text numbers in the United States,

10
00:00:30,725 --> 00:00:33,881
your number also needs
A2P registration first.

11
00:00:33,881 --> 00:00:35,870
We cover that in lesson 14.1.

12
00:00:36,721 --> 00:00:39,887
Reusable messages live
in Marketing, Templates.

13
00:00:39,887 --> 00:00:42,649
Filter by SMS to see your text templates.

14
00:00:42,649 --> 00:00:47,163
You can use them in Conversations,
in bulk sends, and in workflows,

15
00:00:47,163 --> 00:00:51,070
so you write a great message
once and reuse it everywhere.

16
00:00:51,921 --> 00:00:54,398
Click Add template, then Text template.

17
00:00:54,398 --> 00:00:55,732
Give it a clear name.

18
00:00:55,732 --> 00:00:57,256
Then write your message.

19
00:00:57,256 --> 00:01:02,336
Start with Hi, and add the first name
merge field, so every text feels personal.

20
00:01:07,140 --> 00:01:09,641
Watch the counter under the message.

21
00:01:09,641 --> 00:01:15,130
Texts are sent in segments of up to 160
characters, and each segment is billed.

22
00:01:15,130 --> 00:01:18,673
Add an emoji, and a segment
drops to 70 characters.

23
00:01:18,673 --> 00:01:22,981
So keep messages short, and check
the counter before you save.

24
00:01:23,832 --> 00:01:24,926
Now the opt-out.

25
00:01:24,926 --> 00:01:27,456
Add Reply STOP to opt out at the end.

26
00:01:27,456 --> 00:01:32,789
When someone replies STOP, Kyntlo turns
on Do Not Disturb for text messages on

27
00:01:32,789 --> 00:01:36,823
their contact automatically,
so they never get another one.

28
00:01:36,823 --> 00:01:37,917
Then click Save.

29
00:01:38,767 --> 00:01:41,097
WhatsApp works a little differently.

30
00:01:41,097 --> 00:01:45,240
You can reply freely for 24 hours
after a customer messages you.

31
00:01:45,240 --> 00:01:48,930
To start a conversation, or
to message after that window,

32
00:01:48,930 --> 00:01:51,973
you must use a template
that Meta has approved.

33
00:01:52,821 --> 00:01:54,815
Each template shows its status.

34
00:01:54,815 --> 00:01:57,195
Approved templates are ready to send.

35
00:01:57,195 --> 00:02:00,024
Pending ones are still
with Meta for review.

36
00:02:00,024 --> 00:02:04,012
Rejected ones need changes, often
because they look like spam,

37
00:02:04,012 --> 00:02:06,842
with too many capitals
or exclamation marks.

38
00:02:06,842 --> 00:02:08,836
Click a template to preview it.

39
00:02:09,686 --> 00:02:11,549
Now let's send a broadcast.

40
00:02:11,549 --> 00:02:14,241
Go to Contacts, and pick your audience.

41
00:02:14,241 --> 00:02:15,759
A smart list is ideal.

42
00:02:15,759 --> 00:02:21,281
Here, we'll open Invisalign leads, select
everyone with the checkbox at the top,

43
00:02:21,281 --> 00:02:22,661
then click Send SMS.

44
00:02:23,511 --> 00:02:27,230
Write or paste your message,
with the opt-out at the end.

45
00:02:27,230 --> 00:02:28,666
Then choose drip mode.

46
00:02:28,666 --> 00:02:33,495
Instead of texting everyone at once,
Kyntlo sends small batches over time,

47
00:02:33,495 --> 00:02:36,235
so your team can keep up with the replies.

48
00:02:36,235 --> 00:02:40,020
Contacts with Do Not Disturb
on are skipped automatically.

49
00:02:40,870 --> 00:02:44,350
You can follow every bulk
send in the Bulk Actions tab,

50
00:02:44,350 --> 00:02:46,439
including how far a drip has got.

51
00:02:46,439 --> 00:02:50,615
And for messages that should go
out automatically, like reminders,

52
00:02:50,615 --> 00:02:53,906
you'll use workflows, which
we'll build in Module 9.

53
00:02:54,756 --> 00:02:56,081
Here's a pro tip.

54
00:02:56,081 --> 00:03:00,836
Only send broadcasts at sociable
hours, roughly 9 am to 8 pm.

55
00:03:00,836 --> 00:03:07,227
A text at night feels intrusive, and it's
the fastest way to collect STOP replies.

56
00:03:08,082 --> 00:03:10,655
That's text marketing, done the right way.

57
00:03:10,655 --> 00:03:15,677
Next up is the Social Planner, where you'll
schedule posts to Facebook, Instagram,

58
00:03:15,677 --> 00:03:17,821
Google and more, from one calendar.

59
00:03:17,821 --> 00:03:18,679
See you there.
